On 08/08/2010 04:03 AM, Bob LeChevalier wrote:
> We have not had formal minutes for the meetings of the last few
> years, and Robin as Secretary feels that the archived llg-members
> mailing list serves the legal requirement for minutes.  But I would
> like to see some volunteer prepare a concise summary of last year's
> meeting from the archives that resembles earlier meeting minutes,
> which can be approved at the meeting and put on the minutes page, so
> that people can briefly see what happened.  I could use this myself,
> ASAP, to help me prepare.

I've tried to do this. The result can be found on the wiki [1]. I hope
this stuff is all right, I have not had enough education in
legalitybabble to properly do this, I've just copypasted the source from
an olde minutes page and put stuff in that I felt was relevant.


> Ideally, said person will be willing to do this again shortly after
> this year's meeting, and perhaps to use the archives to fill in
> minutes for the missing years.  (This is the sort of thing that can
> demonstrate that you are interested in the stuff that directorship
> entails).  Robin is wearing enough other hats that it would be real
> nice if meeting minutes are not something he has to spend time on.

If the upcoming meeting is similarly uneventful, I should be able to do
that. I am, however, not interested in becomint a director. I am
interested in lojban not exploding due to the general lazyness of big
parts of the community. At least here and there I get little sparks of
motivation and willpower.


